%[text] %[text:anchor:T_DEF03274] # Mass-Spring-Damper Systems
%[text:tableOfContents]{"heading":"**Table of Contents**"}
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_577C7603] ## Scripts
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_E33AF64E] ### [**massSpringDamper.m**](file:./Scripts/massSpringDamper.m)
%[text:table]{"columnWidths":[-1,541],"ignoreHeader":true}
%[text] | ![shock\_absorber\_inset.png](text:image:5f4f) | <p>**In this script, students will...**</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"\bullet"} model a single mass-spring-damper.</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"\bullet"} Turn the damping of a vehicle suspension system.</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"\bullet"} Relate the mass, spring, and damper to their corresponding components in a physical system</p><p></p> |
%[text] | --- | --- |
%[text:table]
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_9A7A74DD] ### [**doubleMassSpringDamper.m**](file:./Scripts/doubleMassSpringDamper.m)
%[text:table]{"columnWidths":[-1,542],"ignoreHeader":true}
%[text] | ![Oscillation3.gif](text:image:0b1b) | <p>**In this script, students will...**</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"\bullet"} model a double mass-spring-damper in Simulink</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"\bullet"} Identify the resonant frequencies present in a two-story building,</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"\bullet"} Use the Symbolic Math Toolbox to help create Simulink models</p><p></p> |
%[text] | --- | --- |
%[text:table]
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_3B719F34] ### [**multipleMassSpringDamper.m**](file:./Scripts/multipleMassSpringDamper.m)
%[text:table]{"columnWidths":[-1,542],"ignoreHeader":true}
%[text] | ![BuidingOscillations.gif](text:image:0b28) | <p>**In this script, students will...**</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"\bullet"} Vectorize a Simulink model for multiple building analysis.</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"\bullet"} Use the spectrum analyzer block to compute the power spectrum.</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"\bullet"} Complete Simulink mass-spring-damper models with n degrees of freedom</p><p></p> |
%[text] | --- | --- |
%[text:table]
